Deliver a message the web UI sends again only once, server side.

While a sandbox starts, the server holds a message's POST open until the
agent can take it. If the connection drops in that time, the server still
delivers the message but the browser sees only a network error, so the web
UI (0024-resend-dropped-message.patch) sends it again with the same
stable_id, and so may the user from the composer. Upstream delivers every
copy: a Claude Code session gets the message typed into its terminal twice.

A message with a stable_id now goes through omnigent_message_resend
(images/server/omnigent_message_resend.py), keyed by session, user,
stable_id and content, after the usual access check. A copy that comes
while the first runs waits for it and gets its answer or error; one that
comes after a success gets its answer for 15 minutes; after a failure the
next copy runs again. An edited resend has other content, so it's
delivered. Messages without a stable_id are handled as before.

The test posts to a claude-native session whose fake runner counts the
prompts it's given.
Base: omnigent v0.15.0 (c8b9b85f822f), after 0016-startup-progress.patch.

